course: dictionary
lesson: 5168
title: Reading a hard word in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long and hard, but the sentence around them often tells you what they mean. «Islamophobia is fear or hatred of Muslims» gives the meaning straight away: it is a fear or hatred aimed at Muslims, people who follow the religion of Islam.
explain: Look at the parts of the word too. Islam is the religion, and -phobia is a word ending that means fear. The dictionary adds that Islamophobia can also mean unfair treatment of Muslims or Islam, so it is more than a feeling. It shows up in how people act.
explain: The second sentence adds an important clue. «Most Muslims reject violence done in the name of Islam» tells you that Muslims themselves are not the problem, and that someone who does harm does not speak for a whole faith. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Islamophobia means hatred, fear or unfair treatment of Muslims or of Islam.
fact: A Muslim is a person who follows the religion of Islam.
fact: The ending -phobia means fear, so a phobia is a strong fear of something.
fact: «Rose sharply» means went up quickly, so the news reports said that hate against Muslims increased fast after 7 October.
fact: Prejudice means judging people unfairly before you know them. Respect means treating everyone fairly, whatever they believe.
exercise: «Islamophobia is fear or hatred of Muslims.» What does Islamophobia mean? | Kindness shown to people of every faith | A type of food eaten at festivals | *Hatred, fear or unfair treatment of Muslims or Islam | A holiday celebrated in the spring
exercise: «News reports said hate against Muslims rose sharply after 7 October.» What does rose sharply mean? | *Went up quickly | Was carried away by the wind | Stayed exactly the same | Fell slowly
exercise: Ayesha says, «Most Muslims reject violence done in the name of Islam.» What does reject mean? | Ask a question politely | Sing loudly in a choir | Eat up every last bit | *Refuse to accept or support
test: The ending -phobia in Islamophobia means what? | Sleep | Love | Food | *Fear
test: Which action shows respect? | Spreading untrue rumours about a religion | Calling someone names because of their religion | Refusing to sit next to a person because of what they believe | *Treating a classmate fairly, whatever faith they follow
exam: Why does the sentence say «most Muslims reject violence done in the name of Islam»? | *To show that people who do harm do not speak for the whole faith | To show that Islam is a brand-new religion | To show that the news is always wrong | To show that all Muslims are dangerous
